WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.078 --> 00:00:09.111
After washing some doll clothes, Nan and Daisy spread them to dry on the grass.

2
00:00:09.112 --> 00:00:12.887
"Let's climb the willow tree," Nan said.

3
00:00:12.888 --> 00:00:17.816
"We can keep an eye on the clothes so they don't blow away."

4
00:00:17.817 --> 00:00:25.697
That summer the old willow tree had become a favorite spot for everyone to sit and chat.

5
00:00:25.698 --> 00:00:32.320
"I hate washing clothes!" Nan said as she settled onto a branch.

6
00:00:32.321 --> 00:00:36.340
"Oh, I don't mind washing at all," Daisy said.

7
00:00:36.341 --> 00:00:41.920
"I like cooking and cleaning and anything that has to do with keeping house.

8
00:00:41.921 --> 00:00:49.107
When I grow up, I'll have a nice house where Demi and I can live together."

9
00:00:49.108 --> 00:00:55.098
"Well, I don't have a brother, and I don't want a house to fuss over," Nan said firmly.

10
00:00:55.099 --> 00:00:58.596
"I'll have an office, where I can work as a doctor.

11
00:00:58.597 --> 00:01:02.527
And when my patients are too sick to visit, I'll make house calls.

12
00:01:02.528 --> 00:01:08.272
Curing folks is my idea of fun—not housekeeping!"

13
00:01:08.273 --> 00:01:19.195
"Ugh!" Daisy made a face and asked, "How can you stand those medicines that smell and taste so nasty?"

14
00:01:19.196 --> 00:01:22.960
"As long as I don't have to take them, they don't bother me.

15
00:01:22.961 --> 00:01:25.628
Besides, they make people well.

16
00:01:25.629 --> 00:01:33.984
Mr. Bauer is teaching me the healing properties of the herbs in my garden, and Mrs. Bauer says I'll be a fine doctor."

17
00:01:33.985 --> 00:01:41.113
Indeed Jo had often mentioned to the professor that Nan had the perfect temperament for a doctor.

18
00:01:41.114 --> 00:01:47.941
She was smart, brave, and felt compassion for anyone sick or in pain.

19
00:01:47.942 --> 00:01:53.636
Jo let Nan assist her whenever any of the boys needed bandaging.

20
00:01:53.637 --> 00:01:59.667
She planned to keep encouraging Nan and her plan to study medicine.

21
00:01:59.668 --> 00:02:05.498
Daisy was still thinking of the more unpleasant aspects of a doctor's life.

22
00:02:05.499 --> 00:02:10.697
"Will you cut off legs and pull out teeth?"

23
00:02:10.698 --> 00:02:15.340
Nan nodded. "I'll do all those things.

24
00:02:15.341 --> 00:02:20.846
My grandpa was a doctor, and I watched him sew a cut on a man's face.

25
00:02:20.847 --> 00:02:25.909
I helped stop the bleeding, and Grandpa said I was very brave."

26
00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:32.976
"How could you do that?" Daisy was amazed at her friend's courage.

27
00:02:32.977 --> 00:02:40.832
"I feel sorry for sick people and want to help them, but I shake at the sight of blood."

28
00:02:40.833 --> 00:02:44.524
"You could be my nurse and cuddle my patients when I have to cut off—"

29
00:02:44.525 --> 00:02:48.986
"Hey, Nan, is that you up there?" called a voice from below.

30
00:02:48.987 --> 00:02:52.608
"I have a splinter in my finger."

31
00:02:52.609 --> 00:02:56.346
Nan looked down and spotted Tommy.

32
00:02:56.347 --> 00:03:00.254
"Climb up, and I'll remove it," she said.

33
00:03:00.255 --> 00:03:05.537
"Though I'm not sure what I'll use for that operation."

34
00:03:05.538 --> 00:03:12.544
By the time Tommy reached them, Daisy had pulled a new packet of sewing needles from her pocket.

35
00:03:12.545 --> 00:03:16.059
"Will one of these work?" she asked.

36
00:03:16.060 --> 00:03:21.225
"I carry them because I never know when I'll need to mend something."

37
00:03:21.226 --> 00:03:28.430
"Perfect!" Nan said, beaming. "Maybe you could be my assistant after all."

38
00:03:28.431 --> 00:03:36.518
"No thanks!" Daisy said, turning her head until Nan had finished removing the splinter.

39
00:03:36.519 --> 00:03:43.298
"All done!" Nan said. "Wash your hands, and you'll be good as new."

40
00:03:43.299 --> 00:03:46.063
"Thanks, Nan!" Tommy said.

41
00:03:46.064 --> 00:03:50.554
"Do you mind if I sit here a minute with you—I'm waiting for Nat."

42
00:03:50.555 --> 00:03:54.605
Nan moved over to make more room for Tommy.

43
00:03:54.606 --> 00:03:58.206
"Hey, Daisy!" Nat called from below.

44
00:03:58.207 --> 00:04:02.745
"Your doll clothes are blowing away!"

45
00:04:02.746 --> 00:04:10.986
Daisy and Nan climbed down to rescue the clothes, and then Nat climbed up to join Tommy.

46
00:04:10.987 --> 00:04:17.350
"So what did you want to talk to me about?" Nat asked, settling into Daisy's spot on the branch.

47
00:04:17.351 --> 00:04:23.691
"I've been thinking we should all pool our money and give Dan something to show our respect for him," Tommy said.

48
00:04:23.692 --> 00:04:28.418
"He was brave to rescue Jack from the birch tree."

49
00:04:28.419 --> 00:04:34.730
"And he was brave to take the blame when everyone suspected me of stealing your money," Nat added.

50
00:04:34.731 --> 00:04:40.246
"Right! Our gift should be something handsome and useful that he'll always remember us by.

51
00:04:40.247 --> 00:04:44.314
So, what do you think I've decided on?" Tommy asked.

52
00:04:44.315 --> 00:04:52.788
"I know he wants a . . . butterfly net," Nat said hesitantly because he wanted to buy that for Dan himself.

53
00:04:52.789 --> 00:04:59.661
"No, a microscope—a good one that he can peer through and see all kinds of tiny things."

54
00:04:59.662 --> 00:05:05.309
"That's perfect," Nat said, glad that Dan was being appreciated.

55
00:05:05.310 --> 00:05:07.984
"But won't it be expensive?"

56
00:05:07.985 --> 00:05:12.529
"Of course it will, but so far everyone I've asked has contributed.

57
00:05:12.530 --> 00:05:17.226
I've already donated my five dollars," Tommy said.

58
00:05:17.227 --> 00:05:23.658
"All your money?" Nat said. "You're the most generous boy I've ever known!"

59
00:05:23.659 --> 00:05:28.911
"Well, I'm tired of the trouble that money causes," Tommy explained.

60
00:05:28.912 --> 00:05:33.791
"From now on, I'm going to give away my cash as fast as I earn it.

61
00:05:33.792 --> 00:05:40.362
That way, no one will try to steal it, and I won't be suspecting innocent people—like you."

62
00:05:40.363 --> 00:05:44.725
"But I thought Mr. Bauer wanted you to save your money."

63
00:05:44.726 --> 00:05:48.514
"I talked to him, and he thought it was a wonderful plan.

64
00:05:48.515 --> 00:05:55.314
He said some of the best men he knew preferred to do good with their money, rather than spending it on themselves."

65
00:05:55.315 --> 00:06:00.567
The two boys sat thinking about that for a few minutes.

66
00:06:00.568 --> 00:06:07.074
It was so quiet and peaceful in the tree that Nat wished he'd brought along his violin.

67
00:06:07.075 --> 00:06:11.016
And that soon gave him an idea.

68
00:06:11.017 --> 00:06:15.294
"You know, I don't really need a new violin," Nat said.

69
00:06:15.295 --> 00:06:21.628
"I could buy Dan a butterfly net, and if there's any money left over, I could donate it to the microscope fund."

70
00:06:21.629 --> 00:06:24.499
"Great!" Tommy said with a grin.

71
00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:28.969
"Let's ask Mr. Bauer if we can go into town together on Monday afternoon.

72
00:06:28.970 --> 00:06:32.780
You could buy the net while I get the microscope."

73
00:06:32.781 --> 00:06:39.216
"Dan's going to be really surprised!" Nat said happily.

